    \item \textbf{Pull before you push.} Always \texttt{git pull origin main} before starting work \emph{and} before pushing. Otherwise merge conflicts.
    \item \textbf{Push small, push often.} Don't sit on a finished file for two days. Push as soon as it works.
    \item \textbf{If a dependency isn't ready, don't wait.} Mock the input, leave a \texttt{TODO} comment, ship. Wire it up properly once the dependency lands.
    \item \textbf{The contracts are the source of truth.} \texttt{docs/schemas.md} and \texttt{docs/api\_contract.md} \textemdash{} if something is ambiguous, reread them. If they're wrong, fix them in a PR and tell the team.
\end{itemize}
\end{tcolorbox}

